  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>Reserve Bank of India, house price index (DBIE report 688), read from India Atlas's archived copy of DBIE; National Housing Bank, RESIDEX dashboards; Bank for International Settlements, residential property prices (WS_SPP, WS_DPP), from India Atlas's archived copy of the BIS statistics. Data vintage <b id="prov-vintage" set:html={TX["prov-vintage"]}></b>.</p>
        <p>Checked by hand: the RBI's 18-city all-India index for January to March 2026, 115.85 here, against 115.9 in the RBI's press release of 29 May 2026 (later revised to 116.2, a revision BIS has not yet picked up).</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Method</h6>
        <p>Values are as published. Changes on a year ago for the RBI and NHB series are computed here from each base's own index; the price of a 646 sq ft flat is NHB's price per square foot times 646. Final RBI values are used where published, provisional otherwise. Zeros that NHB serves for missing values are treated as missing.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions and breaks</h6>
        <p>Three RBI bases (2008-09, 2010-11, 2022-23) and three NHB bases (2012-13, 2017-18, 2024-25) are separate rulers and are never joined here. BIS links the RBI's bases in its own series; that link is BIS's. NHB's back-casts of newer bases into older years are not used.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Version 1.0, built October 2026. Revised each quarter as the RBI, NHB and BIS publish. BIS does not endorse this guide.</p>
      </div>
